# Local Docker test connection and safe model/email defaults. Copy to .env.test.
# The server connection below names no database and E2E_PORT is omitted.
# Stock test:server, test:e2e and test:visual support macOS and Linux/POSIX,
# not Windows. Each omitted database/port setting is allocated per invocation.
# A DATABASE_URL database path and E2E_PORT are independent explicit overrides;
# the environment takes precedence over this file. Explicit databases are reset
# and migrated first, then kept. Generated databases and their scratch databases
# are dropped after supported processes stop, pass or fail or handled SIGINT/TERM.
# The whole project_buddy_e2e_ generated/scratch namespace cannot be pinned.
# Ordinary detached Playwright webServer/browser groups get bounded cooperative
# shutdown and invocation-owned escalation. Unknown ownership is a cleanup
# failure, not permission to kill a port owner or widen signalling authority.
# SIGKILL cannot clean up immediately. Later recovery needs a private journal
# proving the runner and registered supported processes/groups gone, with no
# database connection remaining. Age or the missing runner PID alone is not proof.
# Arbitrary commands deliberately daemonizing, escaping/reparenting before
# registration, stripping the protocol or otherwise evading it are excluded.
# This is not generic arbitrary-descendant containment from portable Node/ps.
# Keep one full web suite scheduled until #475 is accepted and operator setup
# is separately compatible. See README: Invocation-owned local tests.

DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:4444
INVITE_CODE=e2e-test-invite-code
SESSION_SECRET=e2e-test-session-secret
TUTOR_MODEL=mock
EMAIL_TRANSPORT=outbox
EMAIL_OUTBOX_DIR=test-results/email-outbox
